e noun that is not yet identified. Choose by the next sound: an before a vowel sound and a before a consonant sound.","examples":["a uniform","an hourglass"]},{"title":"An identified item","explanation":"Use the when the listener can identify the item, including a second mention. The also works with identified plural nouns.","examples":["I found a ring. The ring was silver.","Please return the borrowed books."]},{"title":"General plural nouns","explanation":"Usually omit the article before a plural noun when referring to its whole class. In these exercises, — means no article.","examples":["Bicycles need regular maintenance.","The bicycles outside are ours."]}],"tips":["Read the full context before choosing.","Check the explanation, including after a correct answer.","A passing practice session is useful feedback, not a language certificate."],"source":"seed","provenance":{"version":"foundations-2026-09-v1","authorship":"Grammacho; generated offline with AI assistance","kind":"original-guidance-aligned","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending","referenceIds":["bc-articles","pcc-esol"],"assessment":"Practice only; levels are approximate teaching labels, not validated CEFR assessment."}}'::jsonb j) payload
